@host = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

# Flow: sync the reading sources from every provider (Olympus + Suwayomi), check what it created,
# then submit an entry on a source the sync linked to Suwayomi so the entry gets hydrated by it.
#
# Needs the backend running and a Suwayomi Server on suwayomi.base-url (default http://localhost:4567)
# with at least one extension installed. The dev database is wiped on every backend restart
# (schema.sql starts with DROP SCHEMA), so run the sync again after restarting.

### Login as the admin seeded by data.sql (the sync is ADMIN-only)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "usernameOrEmail": "admin",
  "password": "admin",
  "rememberMe": false
}

### Sync - no Authorization header -> 401
POST {{host}}/api/moderation/reading-sources/sync

### Sync - first run: creates the sources the providers report, links the ones that already existed
# The report has created / linked / updated / skipped (with a reason) / failedProviders.
# A provider being down shows up in failedProviders without hiding the others.
# @name firstSync
POST {{host}}/api/moderation/reading-sources/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Sync - second run right after: idempotent, nothing created or linked (everything is already matched)
POST {{host}}/api/moderation/reading-sources/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Sync - authenticated but not ADMIN -> 403
# Register and log in as a normal user first (see auth.http), then use that token here.
@userToken = REPLACE_ME
POST {{host}}/api/moderation/reading-sources/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### List - sources the sync created are already APPROVED (an admin installed them in the provider)
# Look for the Suwayomi source you want and copy its id into @suwayomiBackedSourceId below.
GET {{host}}/api/reading-sources?statuses=APPROVED&sortBy=NAME&direction=ASC

### List - moderation view, adds who contributed each source (the admin that ran the sync)
GET {{host}}/api/moderation/reading-sources?statuses=APPROVED
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Import a comic to attach the entry to
# @name importComic
POST {{host}}/api/catalog/myanimelist/2
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Submit - an entry on a Suwayomi-backed source -> 201, hydrated by Suwayomi
# The url must be a work Suwayomi already has stored (it can't resolve a URL it has never seen):
# open or search it once in Suwayomi first. The trailing slash doesn't matter, the provider tries both forms.
# A hydrated response has title, availableChapters and latestChapterAt filled in; if they are null the
# provider failed or was rate limited (one request every 2 s per source) and it is retried on read.
@suwayomiBackedSourceId = REPLACE_ME
# @name submitHydrated
POST {{host}}/api/comics/{{importComic.response.body.$.slug}}/reading-entries
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

{
  "sourceId": {{suwayomiBackedSourceId}},
  "url": "https://www.leercapitulo.co/manga/0wdem0o1jg/level-up-alone",
  "locale": "es-ES"
}

### Submit - same entry again -> 409 (DuplicateComicReadingEntryException)
# Sent twice at the same instant, the second can also be rejected by the database instead:
# 409 with the data-integrity-conflict type.
POST {{host}}/api/comics/{{importComic.response.body.$.slug}}/reading-entries
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

{
  "sourceId": {{suwayomiBackedSourceId}},
  "url": "https://www.leercapitulo.co/manga/0wdem0o1jg/level-up-alone",
  "locale": "es-ES"
}

### List - entries of the comic; stale or unhydrated ones are refreshed through their provider on read
GET {{host}}/api/comics/{{importComic.response.body.$.slug}}/reading-entries
